WEBVTT

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.840
We're entering Wangan.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:42.900
Shifting to high gear using the imported
final gear, revving up to the 8000rpm limit.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:47.410
Ok. Time for the final warm-up.
Let's see if this is the real thing or not.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.720
Here comes the Z. Now all the players are gathered!

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:01.330
<i>Dead End</i>

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:14.320
Right away, there's no tactics, just a straight battle of speed!

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:27.280
A 600hp L-Type Twin Turbo and a 700hp Flat 6 Twin Turbo.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.910
Both are monster machines with high inefficiency.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:33.790
On the other hand, ours is only 450hp.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:42.270
8000rpm at 4th gear. The higher the rev, the lighter it feels!

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:44.000
5th gear.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.970
Until now, revving at 8000rpm at 5th gear, it can reach 265km/h.

00:02:55.970 --> 00:03:01.980
Using the high-geared final upped by 15%,
at 8000rpm and it'll hit 300km/h!

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:06.740
With only just 450hp, we can bring this Lan Evo up to 300km/h!

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.950
It's increasing. The rev is lighter.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:16.810
It's here.

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:17.720
And it's coming fast.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.880
Let's kick off the ground with the power of all four wheels!

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.470
Going up against the corner, this traction!

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:29.470
If we aim for speed, it has to be a four wheel drive!

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:34.760
How's that!

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:39.490
For a two wheel drive, it can only accelerate straight
towards the outer lane from the center f the corner.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:40.820
We're entering from the inner lane!

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:41.990
How fast!

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.260
What an acceleration...

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:51.150
Boss Yamamoto did say so, but is that really only 450hp?

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:55.920
An engine is a really strange thing.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:00.030
There are some parts of it that cannot
be figured out by theory or logic.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:04.420
There are times when some work quite
well even if though it's simply made.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.760
There are those that after putting in a lot of time and effort,

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.930
still don't work well.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.930
With that will you then be satisfied.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:16.930
And what you get before you call it quits.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.930
Oil temperature and pressure check, everything is ok.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.350
What're you going to do?

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:33.160
Accelerate. I'll settle this in one go.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:42.630
<i>It's fast, no, too fast.</i>

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.630
I'll be left behind...

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:56.430
<i>If the BlackBird is a 10, the Lan Evo is a 12 and your Z is barely a 9.</i>

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:57.850
<i>Do you think the difference is big?</i>

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.740
<i>Or can you short it?</i>

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:06.510
<i>That difference can be removed.
It can be better than the same level.</i>

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.910
<i>However, it might end everything in an instant.</i>

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.370
<i>Will you still do it for that Z?</i>

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:21.120
<i>If you desire it, Z will fulfill it, since it chose you as its driver.</i>

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.580
<i>It's that kind of car.</i>

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:32.810
Z is coming!

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:49.990
He got me there, I've been completely overtaken.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.490
That's all you got?

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.740
You must be kidding. I won't let it go.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:08.460
Tominaga-san inserted a special program
into the drive computer, right?

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:09.710
That's right.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:16.230
When the ignition and combustion is at the
limit, boost will be at 1.8bar and over 500hp.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:20.060
But, that can only last for then seconds.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.510
Ten seconds, right?

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:24.360
Ten seconds.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:29.200
That means Tominaga's special program
will break down in ten seconds, right?

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:33.700
In other words, within ten seconds with that power...

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:35.700
is a sudden acceleration.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:38.710
Here I go!

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:53.250
In just a moment, how can it possibly accelerate until this extent?

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.880
What's with such an acceleration?

00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:58.920
It's as if there's not a moment to spare.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:06.910
I just checked, it's just over 4 seconds.

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:08.910
You can still go ahead. Don't withdraw and continue to step!

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.660
As expected, it makes me nervous
bringing the Lan Evo over 200km/h.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:16.620
Because around the short wheel base,
it's not low enough and becomes unstable.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:20.240
It's just your imagination, it's very stable.

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:23.640
Behind us, BlackBird is closing in!

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.840
<i>My first experience witch such acceleration.</i>

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:41.060
<i>Not only just being fast, but an uneasy feeling
that something is going to be exchanged.</i>

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:46.320
<i>This is the ten seconds of my life!</i>

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:02.540
<i>Maki, was I able to teach you important things?</i>

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:07.000
<i>I want to teach you everything I know.</i>

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:12.010
<i>I'm really lucky that I'm still alive after
driving so recklessly all this time.</i>

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:16.880
<i>But there's no guarantee that the same will be applied to you as well.</i>

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:21.270
<i>Now that you've followed my footsteps and started racing...</i>

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:26.260
<i>it's my responsibility that you don't die, no matter what.</i>

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:35.290
<i>Tuners are a contradictory group of people.</i>

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:38.750
<i>Somewhere in their heart, they're hoping for something.</i>

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:42.750
<i>From having the engine that they built with care to break down.</i>

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:47.250
<i>To hoping to understand something based
on what's broken with their creation.</i>

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.710
<i>It's something they can't help out but want to find out.</i>

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:57.930
<i>The persistent pursuit of speed, that is the characteristic of a tuner.</i>

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:16.380
That's it.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:19.990
I can't keep up the tension any more.

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:21.990
It's over.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:26.000
BlackBird got ahead. The Lan Evo has decelerated.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:35.830
If being a pro means finding out by breaking
things again and again, I can't do it.

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:38.460
As I thought, I can't be a pro.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:41.520
I clearly understand...

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.720
that by going all out for that ten seconds, it will break.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:48.720
I can't bear to let that happen.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:52.730
This engine that you assembled is seriously the best.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:57.500
That's why I can't step on any further.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:05.210
<i>If taking the plunge until the end is up
to us, giving up is also our freedom.</i>

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:09.470
<i>If there's any rule to be observed in this area, there's only one.</i>

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:13.170
<i>That is you're free to decide whether to race or give up.</i>

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:17.310
<i>I bet you definitely can never give up.</i>

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:21.460
<i>Since you're crazy over the speed in that area.</i>

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:24.030
<i>You are serious.</i>

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:26.480
<i>When I was 18, I met a machine called car.</i>

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:30.690
<i>And experienced this speed level and this atmosphere.</i>

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:33.680
<i>But I had thought that I would give up one day.</i>

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:40.310
<i>I thought that when the right time comes, I will naturally give up.</i>

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:46.170
<i>That was natural... until I met Z!</i>

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:18.790
<i>While normal cars run at an average of 120km/h,</i>

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:22.070
<i>we slalom with a minimum of 200km/h...</i>

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:27.570
<i>And immediately speed above 250km/h once the road is clear.</i>

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:31.080
<i>With just a slight steering and throttle control,</i>

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:34.320
<i>we suddenly fly over from the first lane to the third lane.</i>

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:39.530
<i>We definitely can't drive like this with unrefined settings.</i>

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:41.950
Z is falling behind.

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:44.040
<i>C1 of the beltway is also not bad.</i>

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:47.560
<i>But it can't be compared to this place after all, definitely.</i>

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.490
<i>It's extraordinary here!</i>

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.020
<i>I cannot withdraw here...</i>

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:59.020
<i>not on this Wangan line!</i>

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:03.440
<i>BlackBird is fast. I will pull away.</i>

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:09.700
A complete victory. The BlackBird is better.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:14.710
The sound is different. The sound of Z has changed.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:18.960
It has never made this kind of noise before. This sound is broken.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.420
Akio-kun...

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:23.500
Even when it's impossible, even when it's not possible anymore...

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:26.390
But still it's trying to run while suffering.

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:28.640
Blow?

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:32.800
No, I don't think it's because something is broken.

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:37.150
It's because of Akio's feeling towards
the race, like something has ended.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:43.580
The long curve to the left after coming out from Kaitei Tunnel.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:47.070
He was doing well until there. He made it this far...

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:52.400
because he wasn't bothered about the disadvantageous
carburetor, but still continuously yearned for speed.

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:56.540
But after he got here, it ended.

00:12:57.370 --> 00:12:59.000
Power against power.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.920
Clearly, he was completely beaten.

00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:09.840
It seems the car that won was BlackBird.

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:12.650
After coming out from Kaitei Tunnel,

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:15.610
Z was left behind at the straight road of Haneda.

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:17.950
That straight road has a steep slope,

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:20.570
so the difference in power showed up, my dad said.

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:25.080
Should I have kept on chasing even if it would blow?

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.450
I'm not sure.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.240
No, that was the end for me.

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:33.190
I think it's important to acknowledge this kind of things.

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:35.500
I guess so.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:42.750
In ten years, you'll be the new boss of RGO.

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:45.180
That's not yet...

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:48.460
Experience many things and become a good tuner.

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:51.140
I'll keep on watching you from Osaka.

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:56.360
Watching? How could you do that?
A photo published in the newspaper?

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:58.720
Or on RGO's homepage?

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:03.490
I wonder how good this observation of yours is going to be.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:07.230
In the end, you won't know anything unless you see it directly!

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:12.750
Isn't it better if we stop contact after you go back to Osaka?

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:17.820
Since you'll be going back to Osaka.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.660
To Osaka, where there are people waiting for you.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:42.690
Hello, I'm packing my things now.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:45.660
Well, most of them will be thrown away though.

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:48.200
I'll go back there tomorrow.

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:50.630
Yes, that's right.

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:55.260
It's not three months yet, but it's alright now.

00:14:56.300 --> 00:15:00.210
Well, I could sort of understand and be satisfied with myself.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:05.710
I really enjoyed myself, racing with genuine racers.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:14.250
<i>The hesitant feeling which I've kept all this time has disappeared,</i>

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:18.630
<i>and I felt I was taught, or more like I was saved.</i>

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:22.600
<i>I understand the meaning of racing a little more, too.</i>

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:29.600
<i>Maki, we're not brothers from the same mother.</i>

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:34.320
<i>I was so fixated on this that I missed what was most important.</i>

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:39.040
<i>Once I return, I'll tell you properly, about my true feelings.</i>

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:49.400
Yama-chan looks pretty down...

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:50.810
Yeah, me as well...

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:54.610
I wonder if Eiji is going back to his previous work.

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:56.310
Probably.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:05.720
Eiji has gone back to Osaka, right?

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:13.690
W-What?

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:15.750
Since you're properly covered with fat,

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:19.590
it can't be seen at a glance but there's
no doubt there are string muscles inside.

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:23.890
After ten years, it will become an arm with properly toned muscles.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:28.530
What are you going to do? Are you
seriously going to follow in my footsteps?

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:33.060
I don't know yet. For the time being,
I think I just enjoy assembling engines.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:36.060
I envy you.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:41.760
Why? Mama said that nobody has lived
as much as he liked, like you did.

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:43.510
True to say though,

00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:48.970
but there are times when I can't help but envy your generation.

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:53.730
After I realized I could only live in my
own generation, which was not surprising.

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:57.740
The same goes for cars.

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:02.700
No matter how good the performance of
any car, it can't be at center stage forever.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.040
Human beings are also the same.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:09.780
No matter how good a sports player is, one
day he'll still become a person of the past.

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:12.700
The passage of time is cruel but honest.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:16.940
You'll live in your own generation.

00:17:16.940 --> 00:17:20.180
If it's as a tuner, I'll be happy and also envy you.

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:31.190
This R32...

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:33.780
Yo! It's been a while.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:36.190
Hello!

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:42.480
I've heard lots of rumors, at last Z was beaten by BlackBird.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:45.040
It wasn't because of a blow, Gacchan.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:47.530
As after that, it seemed to run normally again.

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:52.340
That's right, it's as fast as before. But...

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:55.830
<i>Something's different after all.</i>

00:17:56.320 --> 00:18:00.540
<i>The feel of its movement... although Z is still Z.</i>

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:07.510
Feels like something has been lost, that's what Akio-kun said.

00:18:07.510 --> 00:18:13.470
<i>Something</i> I see... but if something's wrong
with it, it can't be fixed unless it is dismantled,

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:16.380
as long as that Z is a machine.

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:20.290
You really like him that much?

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:24.780
Just be honest and tell him. You like him, right?

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:28.300
I wonder how I should say it...

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:31.800
You should stop chasing him.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:35.300
You'll lose yourself.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:39.540
He's crazy for speed, he won't ever pay any attention to girls.

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:42.300
Even though you just wait for him quietly, nothing will change.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:46.810
It's ok even if nothing changes.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:51.360
What are you saying?! You're being too good! Right, Yamamoto?

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:54.820
I'm not sure. Her being a good girl is for sure though.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:58.810
Seriously! Quit trying to be a nice middle-age uncle!

00:18:59.390 --> 00:19:04.280
It's really fine as it is now. Akio-kun should stay just the way he is.

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:09.830
But thank you for your concern. Sasaki-san, you're really kind.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:14.590
What?! Well, not really...

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:17.810
Gacchan is, if anything, disgusting, right?

00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:19.810
Shut up, Yamamoto!

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:28.350
By the way, you appear on TV, right? On Drive-something.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:29.810
Drive Go Go?

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:36.190
Right, that's the one. I didn't know it at all but the
one who appears together with you is Kijima, right?

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:37.930
Do you know him?

00:19:37.930 --> 00:19:44.070
Yes, he claims to be a car commentator
now, but he was quite the racer last time.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.070
That Kijima-san!?

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:49.230
"The Big Mouth Slugger".

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:52.570
Next time, if there's a chance, do bring him over here.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:57.740
Drive Go! Go!

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:02.810
Continuing from last week, this week we'll talk about the 911 too.

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:05.050
Reina-chan, do you like the 911?

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:08.000
Yes, among foreign cars I like it best.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:13.020
Reina-chan's fans, did you hear that? Fans should check out the 911.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:18.810
Kijima-san!

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:21.100
Hi, Reina-chan.

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:25.560
You drove the Porsche, today? What happened to the usual one?

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:27.070
This is a demo car.

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:30.400
Since I always promote it in the show.

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:33.790
I wonder if I'll be able to drive it?

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:37.960
Sure, no problem. But you have an R, right?

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:40.840
Yes. Kijima-san, can you let me drive it for a bit?

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:43.300
Sure, go ahead.

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:49.060
It's good as expected.

00:20:55.760 --> 00:20:58.980
But is a normal Porsche like this?

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:05.490
Kijima-san, if it's alright with you, there's a place I'd like to drop by.

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:15.420
Oh? They're here! She seriously brought him here!

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:21.720
Yo! It's been a while, how are you Kijima?

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:25.720
Sasaki-san... Yamamoto-san!

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:30.760
I see... what's profitable are foreign cars as expected.

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:34.100
Probably, because they have culture and backbone.

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:37.190
Culture? Just like before, you still talk big.

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:41.140
You always backed your words with figures, since long ago.

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:47.850
It's already time? I'm sorry, maybe we can catch up another time.

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:53.450
I have a draft I must prepare by tonight.

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:56.620
I'm really sorry, since we were able to meet after such a long time...

00:21:59.850 --> 00:22:03.290
Say, Kijima, what happened to that FC?

00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:09.420
That white FC3S which you were
absorbed with when you were still in Zero.

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:15.260
Sometimes we still talk about it.

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:17.110
Like what happened to it,

00:22:17.110 --> 00:22:19.460
because witch such a level of tuning, it's not like anybody can simply drive it.

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:21.780
I was a great car.

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:24.840
A 2-rotor 13B doing a complete round at C7.

00:22:24.840 --> 00:22:27.940
You can output about 500hp with the final Tsukuba Attack, right?

00:22:29.040 --> 00:22:32.580
I don't know anything about it anymore.

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:35.000
Or more like, I don't have any interest in it anymore.

00:22:38.430 --> 00:22:40.620
I've got nothing to do with that kind of world anymore.

00:22:41.370 --> 00:22:43.950
The "Big Mouth Slugger" is no more.

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:01.430
Good evening, sorry to visit so late.

00:23:01.430 --> 00:23:03.700
No problem. Looking for something?

00:23:03.700 --> 00:23:05.340
Yes, Rikako-san.

00:23:05.970 --> 00:23:06.660
Rikako?

00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:09.650
I want her to take a look at this Z.

00:23:11.100 --> 00:23:12.180
Z?
